<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vilaine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vilaine is the longest river of Brittany in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, flowing about 220 km from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayenne">Mayenne</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rennes">Rennes</a>, where it is joined by the Ille, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a>. Together with the Ille it gives its name to the department of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ille-et-vilaine">Ille-et-Vilaine</a>. In ancient times its basin was the territory of the Gaulish Redones.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vilaine.jpg" alt="Vilaine" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:XIIIfromTOKYO · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Vilaine_%C3%A0_Rennes.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
